cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on these experiments, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ITASORL: Incidental Detection of Surrogate Worlds by a From-Scratch Digital Organism"
authors:
  - family-names: "Tate"
    given-names: "Levy"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1337-0709"
repository-code: "https://github.com/iLevyTate/ItaSoRL"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  ITASORL measures whether a recurrent agent trained from scratch, with no
  imported semantic knowledge and no reward for detection, comes to carry in its
  state whether its world runs on authentic base dynamics or a substrate-flawed
  surrogate, set against how detectable the flaw is to a privileged detector at a
  stated detector-side noise. Hand-authored flaws (L1 discretization, L2 rollout
  drift) are detectable but did not meet the registered encoding criterion; at
  the L3 gate's detector noise the L2 flaws read 0.62 to 0.65, so the matched
  contrast is L1 against L3. A learned-dynamics fingerprint (L3) met the
  criterion for survival-trained agents carrying a next-observation auxiliary at
  the registered 300-update budget, and a per-timestep linear behavior control
  leaves most of the signal. At that budget the agent without the auxiliary did
  not meet it (0.601, device-controlled); the same arm at 450 updates did, with a
  failed skill match, so the auxiliary result is bounded by budget. An
  independently trained fingerprint keeps the survival-specific margin under the
  bar (0.639). The direction reads a capacity variant of the same recipe and a
  random-Fourier-features law fit on the same data; the reverse direction fails.
  A common-garden control, re-scored with a corrected estimator, passes the
  frozen rule on both directions (forward 0.666, reverse 0.684): prefix condition
  remains decodable after restoring authentic dynamics, without separating
  memory from a physical footprint (see FINDINGS section 10.6.1). All
  survival-trained numbers above come from a trainer whose GAE truncation
  bootstrap was corrected in October 2026; they are historical until the
  corrected confirmation runs replace them (docs/CORRECTIONS.md).
keywords:
  - artificial-life
  - reinforcement-learning
  - self-supervised-learning
  - simulation-hypothesis
  - world-models
